1
00:00:01,630 --> 00:00:04,190
Oh, right, you came for the wake.

2
00:00:04,930 --> 00:00:08,030
Grandma's house has been 
left unattended since she died.

3
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:11,370
I'm considering selling it,

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:15,240
I do come clean
every now and then

5
00:00:11,370 --> 00:00:13,610
but I need to get it in order first.

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,240
Before calling
the pros

7
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:15,240
It'd be nice to have a guy's help.

8
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:16,550
Sure.

9
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:18,410
Sorry to ask you on your day off.

10
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:19,080
Nah.

11
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:21,380
I was just sitting around watching WeTube.

12
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:25,950
We're here.

13
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:29,090
Ichinose

14
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:30,870
This is it.

15
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:13,390
I thought I was good at going it alone

16
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:13,390
Would you prefer to go together?

17
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:40,920
Place
your finger here

18
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:02,060
Rent-a-Girlfriend

19
00:02:04,230 --> 00:02:07,980
"Childhood Home and Girlfriend"

20
00:02:05,310 --> 00:02:08,320
The front door's locked. 
Mind if we go in from the back?

21
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:09,570
S-Sure.

22
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:13,090
<i>This is Mizuhara's childhood home.</i>

23
00:02:12,110 --> 00:02:13,530
Haven't been here
since the wake

24
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:16,740
<i>It didn't really hit me the last time.</i>

25
00:02:17,490 --> 00:02:22,080
And I was only here
for a minute

26
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:22,080
<i>Depending on how you slice it, this may 
be more valuable than her apartment.</i>

27
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:24,470
<i>She's doing her investigation,</i>

28
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:26,920
key

29
00:02:24,470 --> 00:02:26,920
<i>so she invited me to 
a more personal space?</i>

30
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,920
key...

31
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:28,810
<i>This feels tense!</i>

32
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:30,630
Chills down the neck

33
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:30,960
<i>Like I'm going to meet her parents!</i>

34
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,900
Please let me have your daughter!

35
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,880
You're asking the front door?

36
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,820
Oh, that cover...

37
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:42,850
The water main

38
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,790
It's loose, so be careful.

39
00:02:40,870 --> 00:02:42,850
This thing is always so heavy.

40
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:45,310
And... hup!

41
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,270
Come on in.

42
00:02:50,510 --> 00:02:53,080
Sorry, the slippers are by the entrance.

43
00:02:51,690 --> 00:02:54,610
Excuse me

44
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,610
Don't worry about it.

45
00:02:56,670 --> 00:02:57,450
<i>Wha?</i>

46
00:02:57,780 --> 00:02:59,410
<i>The washing machine's ancient!</i>

47
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:04,130
<i>The creaking of the floor, 
and the scent of bedding and incense...</i>

48
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:03,340
The second floor's this way, 
and that's the entrance.

49
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:06,370
If you want
to use it

50
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:05,220
The bathroom's next to the entrance.

51
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:06,370
O-Okay.

52
00:03:07,070 --> 00:03:09,080
<i>This feels so lived-in.</i>

53
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:13,300
<i>It's a lot older than I expected.</i>

54
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:13,300
It's frankly run-down

55
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:17,320
The air gets stale when it's been 
closed up for two months, huh?

56
00:03:13,970 --> 00:03:17,800
<i>It doesn't suit Mizuhara's 
current image at all.</i>

57
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:18,140
This 
glamorous 
girl

58
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,540
Better air the place out.

59
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:22,100
<i>Not that I can tell her that.</i>

60
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:24,150
This is the living room.

61
00:03:24,150 --> 00:03:25,310
Before the pros show up,

62
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:28,600
I want to put all the 
miscellaneous trinkets in boxes.

63
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,600
Height matters

64
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:31,110
I want to take down the curtains, too.

65
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,310
<i>Wait, what?</i>

66
00:03:30,890 --> 00:03:33,280
<i>Rocks? Why are there rocks?</i>

67
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:36,240
They're not pickle weights...

68
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:36,240
<i>And they're all over the place.</i>

69
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:36,240
It's not some
big bonsai, right?

70
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:36,240
staaare...

71
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:36,240
Locks eyes with the rocks

72
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:39,220
<i>Can I ask about this?</i>

73
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,530
R-Rocks?

74
00:03:39,990 --> 00:03:41,530
All the courage he could muster

75
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:46,120
Yeah, it's crazy, right? 
That's my grandpa's collection.

76
00:03:47,390 --> 00:03:50,830
Any time he'd travel anywhere for work, 
he'd bring rocks from there.

77
00:03:47,670 --> 00:03:50,830
Saying each one
was a memory

78
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:53,590
There's a bunch in the yard, too.

79
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:57,680
The stuff inside's the tip
of the iceberg, actually

80
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:57,680
This is all

81
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:57,680
I'd like you to gather them outside to 
make it easy for the trash collectors.

82
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:57,680
This is what I need
the most help with

83
00:03:57,950 --> 00:04:00,720
O-Oh, really?

84
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:02,410
<i>His collection?</i>

85
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:04,770
There's a lot

86
00:04:02,410 --> 00:04:04,770
<i>I see why you'd want 
a guy's help for this.</i>

87
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:08,230
But they're mementos...

88
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:08,230
and you're
dumping them?

89
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:08,230
I'll do the job, but...

90
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:06,800
Are you sure, though?

91
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:08,230
Will you keep them in
your Room 203, then?

92
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,230
What else am I supposed to do?

93
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:11,440
<i>Not very sentimental, is she?</i>

94
00:04:08,770 --> 00:04:11,440
Yeah, no

95
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,440
I guess it is what it is

96
00:04:11,850 --> 00:04:14,060
Let me show you the other rooms.

97
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:15,210
Th-Thanks.

98
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:18,360
Okay, shall we begin?

99
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:20,570
beam beam

100
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:20,570
<i>We're working as one!</i>

101
00:04:18,650 --> 00:04:20,570
I'll do my best

102
00:04:21,190 --> 00:04:24,240
I'll sort out what's needed 
and what isn't while I clean.

103
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:28,460
Let's start with the tough one—
the living room

104
00:04:24,590 --> 00:04:27,080
You start dealing with 
the final boss, the rocks.

105
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:28,460
Put the trash in
the bags over here

106
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:28,460
Roger

107
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,460
Final boss?

108
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:31,940
My grandma was such a hoarder.

109
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:37,090
<i>Where am I looking, 
and in her family home, no less?!</i>

110
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:37,090
Her ancestors
are watching!!

111
00:04:37,590 --> 00:04:42,140
<i>This is really some situation, though.</i>

112
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:44,940
<i>We're in her family home all alone.</i>

113
00:04:42,790 --> 00:04:46,230
Sheesh, it gets covered in dust so easily.

114
00:04:44,940 --> 00:04:47,380
<i>It's like I'm her childhood 
friend or something.</i>

115
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:50,600
<i>Is that how much she's opening up to me?</i>

116
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:53,320
<i>We're all alone here right now!</i>

117
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:55,690
Make me and my background all yours.

118
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:57,560
You've grown up so much.

119
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:01,200
<i>Focus on your work, you dumbass!</i>

120
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:01,200
There's a lot of rocks

121
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:03,920
What're you spacing out for?

122
00:05:03,410 --> 00:05:07,950
Carry them out

123
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,600
Huh? Oh, sorry.

124
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,950
Wait, why are you sweating 
so much already?

125
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:09,790
<i>Don't get so conscious of her!</i>

126
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:12,000
I am but a forklift

127
00:05:12,630 --> 00:05:16,630
<i>Damn, the bath's super old-fashioned, too.</i>

128
00:05:16,630 --> 00:05:20,550
<i>I've only ever seen bathrooms 
like this in old TV shows.</i>

129
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:24,010
<i>Mizuhara lived her life here
for the longest time, huh?</i>

130
00:05:24,180 --> 00:05:25,720
<i>Wait, for a long time?</i>

131
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:25,720
Lived her life here?

132
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:28,140
<i>Which means high schooler Mizuhara...</i>

133
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:29,620
<i>bathed here?</i>

134
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:33,160
I need to make myself pretty 
for the one I'll meet someday.

135
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:37,450
<i>Gyaaargh!</i>

136
00:05:35,910 --> 00:05:38,540
Huh? That sounded like 
you dropped something!

137
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:41,550
I-It's okay. I dropped it on my feet.

138
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:45,490
I can't! It's sensory overload!!

139
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:43,820
Did you really think there 
wouldn't be a bathroom?

140
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:50,080
Keep

141
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:50,080
Keep

142
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:50,080
Dump

143
00:05:56,790 --> 00:06:00,340
No one ever said
it would be this hard...

144
00:05:57,710 --> 00:06:00,340
<i>This is actually hard labor!</i>

145
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:03,840
<i>Who brings home rocks? 
What was her grandpa even like?</i>

146
00:06:00,630 --> 00:06:03,840
Way to trouble
your family!!

147
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:03,840
Think of the
consequences!!

148
00:06:04,490 --> 00:06:08,260
<i>But she really is so blasé about it.</i>

149
00:06:06,890 --> 00:06:11,430
I mean, not like
there's a better option

150
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:11,430
<i>I'm sure her grandpa 
did care a lot about these.</i>

151
00:06:12,210 --> 00:06:18,400
<i>Normally, you'd get a bit sentimental 
cleaning up an empty family home.</i>

152
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:23,360
<i>She's always calm and logical, 
and she never lets her emotions win.</i>

153
00:06:24,110 --> 00:06:29,200
<i>Will I ever capture 
this iron maiden's heart?</i>

154
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:31,080
I'll give it a real shot.

155
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:36,130
Do it for her!!

156
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:36,130
Don't show any
signs of fatigue!

157
00:06:33,710 --> 00:06:36,130
<i>Still, I just gotta do it!</i>

158
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:46,840
You brought another rock?

159
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:48,970
From Iyo in Ehime!

160
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:52,180
Beat.

161
00:06:48,890 --> 00:06:52,180
Midnight

162
00:06:48,970 --> 00:06:52,180
A 20-hour, 20-minute round trip!

163
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:56,410
Please don't make it heavier 
based on distance.

164
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:56,900
That's not even a rock!
It's a boulder!

165
00:06:56,940 --> 00:07:04,280
Long-distance drives

166
00:06:57,210 --> 00:07:01,140
Ooh, that hits the back hard.

167
00:06:59,530 --> 00:07:01,790
You need to lie down.

168
00:06:59,570 --> 00:07:04,280
I'll put a compress on you

169
00:07:01,690 --> 00:07:04,280
You'll throw it
out again, you know?

170
00:07:01,790 --> 00:07:04,280
Don't push yourself. 
You're not young anymore.

171
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:05,880
That's right.

172
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:09,580
You could turn down clients 
demanding such long-distance trips.

173
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:14,970
What? They're heading far away 
late at night with no travel options.

174
00:07:14,970 --> 00:07:16,850
They all have their reasons.

175
00:07:18,830 --> 00:07:21,720
Not that I think I'm being 
a hero or anything...

176
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:27,460
but for people in need, I can always 
find the strength to fight through!

177
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:40,310
Almost done.

178
00:07:42,110 --> 00:07:43,530
Just noticed

179
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:43,530
<i>An altar?</i>

180
00:07:44,430 --> 00:07:47,110
<i>Photos. That's her grandpa.</i>

181
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:49,020
<i>That means...</i>

182
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:52,350
<i>this one must be...</i>

183
00:07:52,350 --> 00:07:53,930
Oh, that's my mom.

184
00:07:55,090 --> 00:08:00,420
But she died when I was four, 
so I barely remember anything about her.

185
00:08:00,770 --> 00:08:03,860
She didn't like taking 
photographs, it seems.

186
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:06,230
That's about all we had left of her.

187
00:08:07,730 --> 00:08:09,970
<i>This is Mizuhara's mom.</i>

188
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:12,890
<i>She was really beautiful.</i>

189
00:08:12,890 --> 00:08:15,430
<i>No surprise there. 
She was Sayuri-san's daughter.</i>

190
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:17,670
Okay, back to work.

191
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:19,140
It's gotten dark

192
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:19,140
R-Right.

193
00:08:19,990 --> 00:08:23,610
<i>She really is so chill about it all.</i>

194
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:27,080
<i>It makes sense, given she was 
only four at the time.</i>

195
00:08:30,590 --> 00:08:32,900
I think we did a pretty good job.

196
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:38,500
A sense of pride
and accomplishment!!

197
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:35,390
I carried out all the rocks.

198
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:38,500
I've learned not to collect 
rocks when I'm older.

199
00:08:36,830 --> 00:08:38,500
Not me

200
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:41,180
It's so much cleaner now! Thanks!

201
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:41,840
Mwah!

202
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:45,340
Yeah, not happening

203
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:45,340
Rock

204
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:49,510
<i>This is Granny Sayuri's room.</i>

205
00:08:51,510 --> 00:08:52,680
<i>Mizuhara.</i>

206
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:56,080
<i>A photo album?</i>

207
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:58,400
Oh, you're all done?

208
00:08:56,890 --> 00:08:59,690
Over there?

209
00:08:58,400 --> 00:08:59,690
Y-Yeah.

210
00:08:59,970 --> 00:09:02,150
Really? Thanks a lot.

211
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:04,610
No problem.

212
00:09:10,310 --> 00:09:12,190
Photo album, huh?

213
00:09:12,110 --> 00:09:13,780
I found an album

214
00:09:12,190 --> 00:09:13,780
I was sorting out the books,

215
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,920
but this one...

216
00:09:16,850 --> 00:09:19,680
I just couldn't bring myself to dump it.

217
00:09:21,950 --> 00:09:23,880
<i>Of course.</i>

218
00:09:25,110 --> 00:09:26,960
We're so weird as a species.

219
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:29,790
I don't remember a thing about her,

220
00:09:29,790 --> 00:09:34,930
but just because she was my mother, 
I can't throw away any pictures of her.

221
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:42,390
I guess the one thing she's taught me 
is to take photos with my kids.

222
00:09:43,210 --> 00:09:45,440
<i>So she does miss her mom.</i>

223
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:51,450
<i>Duh. I know it's Mizuhara, 
but there's no way she isn't lonely.</i>

224
00:09:51,990 --> 00:09:54,930
<i>But she's doing all she can 
to look forward.</i>

225
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:57,760
It's not weird at all.

226
00:09:59,910 --> 00:10:02,830
She's your mother. 
It's natural to feel that way.

227
00:10:06,590 --> 00:10:09,550
stare...

228
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:07,890
Stare.

229
00:10:08,090 --> 00:10:09,550
Wait, what?

230
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:12,510
Yeah?

231
00:10:13,930 --> 00:10:15,430
Cute...

232
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:19,220
I wasn't fishing for sympathy, okay?

233
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:22,020
Even without a mom, I've had a good life.

234
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:24,730
Well, as thanks for giving birth to me,

235
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:28,440
I guess I could give her lifetime access 
to a photo frame and display spot.

236
00:10:25,770 --> 00:10:28,440
On my shelf

237
00:10:26,270 --> 00:10:28,440
Good for you, Mom

238
00:10:30,590 --> 00:10:32,280
<i>I want to give her a hug.</i>

239
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:36,360
<i>Listen, Mizuhara! I'm serious about you!</i>

240
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:40,990
<i>I wanna be there for you for life, 
no matter what I have to give up!</i>

241
00:10:41,330 --> 00:10:45,290
<i>Your loneliness, sorrow, 
strength, and weakness...</i>

242
00:10:45,290 --> 00:10:47,460
<i>I'll embrace your everything.</i>

243
00:10:47,890 --> 00:10:52,760
They all fill the void in their heart 
 with work or significant others.

244
00:10:53,130 --> 00:10:55,120
<i>Can I not do that for you?</i>

245
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:57,200
<i>Can't it be me?</i>

246
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,860
Huh? An earthquake?

247
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:09,270
Whoa, it's a big one.

248
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,940
Hey, watch out!

249
00:11:29,850 --> 00:11:31,290
<i>Y-Yikes!</i>

250
00:11:31,710 --> 00:11:33,630
I'll get off!

251
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:33,630
It's not what you think! 
I didn't mean to...

252
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:34,340
Wait.

253
00:11:37,550 --> 00:11:38,550
Wait.

254
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:47,030
Rent-a-Girlfriend

255
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:53,440
<i>Whoa, what's all this?</i>

256
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:55,280
<i>"Wait"?</i>

257
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:57,940
<i>I lost my balance and landed on her,</i>

258
00:11:57,940 --> 00:12:00,990
<i>and I thought she'd send me flying.</i>

259
00:12:01,350 --> 00:12:04,140
<i>But she stopped me from getting off!</i>

260
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,700
<i>Why, though? For what reason?</i>

261
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:08,230
<i>She's so tiny!</i>

262
00:12:08,230 --> 00:12:12,980
<i>So frail that I feel like 
she wouldn't fight me off.</i>

263
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:16,210
<i>Is she okay with taking me in?</i>

264
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,520
<i>Mizuhara...</i>

265
00:12:19,870 --> 00:12:21,620
<i>Mizuhara!</i>

266
00:12:28,670 --> 00:12:30,010
You've got a leaf on you.

267
00:12:32,850 --> 00:12:35,340
Oh, I did? My bad.

268
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:37,360
Sorry I was dirty

269
00:12:35,340 --> 00:12:37,360
Anyway, I took out all the rocks.

270
00:12:37,740 --> 00:12:40,720
But there's still cleaning to do, 
so I'll get back to it.

271
00:12:41,950 --> 00:12:45,250
<i>Grargh! I was this close to exploding!</i>

272
00:12:44,990 --> 00:12:48,410
It was just like
some manga

273
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:48,410
<i>What was with the "wait"? 
What was with the clinging?!</i>

274
00:12:48,410 --> 00:12:51,180
<i>A leaf? Really?</i>

275
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:54,410
<i>I didn't have anything like that 
on me when I checked!</i>

276
00:12:54,410 --> 00:12:56,670
<i>She was acting strange, too!</i>

277
00:12:56,670 --> 00:12:59,380
<i>Was that part of her investigation?</i>

278
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:01,720
<i>This is hard! By which I mean </i>I'm<i> hard!</i>

279
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:05,810
<i>Rawr! A leaf! It had to be a leaf!</i>

280
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:05,810
There was nothing
more than that!!!

281
00:13:18,670 --> 00:13:22,040
That wasn't a very good excuse, was it?

282
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:32,210
Hisakata

283
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:31,100
Thanks for the help. 
I'll pay you for it soon.

284
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,210
It's fine.

285
00:13:32,210 --> 00:13:34,420
No, it's not.

286
00:13:34,850 --> 00:13:39,020
<i>I can't believe I went to 
Mizuhara's family home.</i>

287
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:40,510
It was just for
a few hours, but

288
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:40,510
<i>Who'd believe that?</i>

289
00:13:40,890 --> 00:13:44,500
<i>I was in her family home, 
and I got to see her there.</i>

290
00:13:43,390 --> 00:13:47,970
I don't like it when people say, 
"It's still cold out in April."

291
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:47,970
<i>I feel like I've found a new side to her.</i>

292
00:13:47,970 --> 00:13:50,140
It's like this every year.

293
00:13:48,970 --> 00:13:50,930
<i>But at the same time,</i>

294
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:55,770
<i>I realized there must be so much 
to her that I have no idea about.</i>

295
00:13:56,350 --> 00:13:59,160
<i>Did her investigation get anywhere?</i>

296
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:03,490
<i>Going to her family home just 
put my imagination into overdrive.</i>

297
00:14:04,270 --> 00:14:06,800
<i>If only we could be a family together...</i>

298
00:14:07,910 --> 00:14:11,910
<i>I want to know more about her! 
I want to get to know her much better!</i>

299
00:14:12,370 --> 00:14:15,250
Do you have, like, an ideal 
image of a married couple?

300
00:14:15,830 --> 00:14:16,610
Huh?

301
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,470
I dunno. Do you?

302
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:23,260
Never thought
about it

303
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:26,970
<i>Ugh! I hadn't thought about it, either!</i>

304
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:26,970
Think about it first,

305
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:26,970
dude!!

306
00:14:26,970 --> 00:14:29,770
Oh, uh, I dunno!

307
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:34,940
Loud

308
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:32,160
A couple who are lovey-dovey 
until the day they die?

309
00:14:29,890 --> 00:14:34,940
Super!!

310
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:34,940
And I mean
super, super!!

311
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:34,940
Like, they never fight or something.

312
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:37,400
<i>How many points does that score?</i>

313
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:40,860
Lovey-dovey, huh? 
I guess that makes sense.

314
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:42,760
<i>Did I pass?</i>

315
00:14:41,150 --> 00:14:43,820
Lovey-dovey
with Mizuhara...♥

316
00:14:42,610 --> 00:14:43,820
Simple mind

317
00:14:44,490 --> 00:14:48,360
But I think I'd want something different.

318
00:14:48,330 --> 00:14:49,280
Failed?!

319
00:14:49,710 --> 00:14:52,480
A couple used to be strangers at first.

320
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:56,000
There's no way they'd have 
the exact same values.

321
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,800
Nobody's perfect,

322
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:02,380
so I'm sure they'd fight and get 
on each other's nerves at times.

323
00:15:03,750 --> 00:15:04,800
But...

324
00:15:06,790 --> 00:15:11,420
if something fun happened seconds later, 
they should be able to laugh about it.

325
00:15:11,420 --> 00:15:13,260
That's the kind of family I want to be.

326
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,690
<i>Mizuhara...</i>

327
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:20,440
<i>Mizuhara.</i>

328
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:22,770
I think I'll go with that, too.

329
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:27,070
You just convinced me!

330
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:41,250
What the heck? You're so silly!

331
00:15:45,050 --> 00:15:47,020
Talk about easily influenced.

332
00:15:45,790 --> 00:15:48,680
<i>I'll probably never forget this day 
for the rest of my life.</i>

333
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:48,680
L-Lay off!

334
00:15:49,210 --> 00:15:54,520
<i>I went to her family home, 
and it had all this history.</i>

335
00:15:55,130 --> 00:15:59,480
<i>While I was there, I could imagine 
the way she'd lived her life.</i>

336
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:01,340
<i>I want to be with her,</i>

337
00:16:02,050 --> 00:16:03,350
<i>and be there for her.</i>

338
00:16:04,140 --> 00:16:08,910
<i>It was more than enough to make me want 
to see what it'd be like to live with her.</i>

339
00:16:10,590 --> 00:16:12,370
We're finally home.

340
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:14,670
That was a lot of work...

341
00:16:15,380 --> 00:16:16,360
Huh?

342
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:23,800
Wait, what's going on here?

343
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:27,130
<i>What's this? That's a lot of people.</i>

344
00:16:27,830 --> 00:16:28,950
There you are.

345
00:16:28,950 --> 00:16:30,000
Mini-chan?

346
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,720
Wait, you were together?

347
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,720
Where'd you run off to now?

348
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:35,350
Huh? Oh, it's not like that.

349
00:16:35,350 --> 00:16:38,040
We just ran into each other.

350
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,060
<i>Look at her lie.</i>

351
00:16:40,310 --> 00:16:43,520
Anyway, what's going on? 
This doesn't look good at all.

352
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:47,490
Looks like we can't go 
into the building anymore!

353
00:16:47,490 --> 00:16:48,660
What?!

354
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:50,320
Wait, what does that mean?

355
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:54,350
It seems the whole building 
started cracking everywhere.

356
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:58,160
The landlord came to each room, 
asking us to evacuate.

357
00:16:58,160 --> 00:17:02,700
It's an old building, so it didn't have 
the latest quake resistance.

358
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:05,780
The gas and power lines are fine,

359
00:17:04,210 --> 00:17:08,260
He said it was a
good time to rebuild

360
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:08,260
but it's really not livable, it seems.

361
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:10,820
<i>Cracks? Resistance?</i>

362
00:17:08,550 --> 00:17:12,760
Hence
the fire truck

363
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:12,510
I knew it was run-down,
but I had no idea
it was this bad!!

364
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:13,010
<i>Not livable? Are you kidding me?</i>

365
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,720
It was fine
all this time

366
00:17:13,010 --> 00:17:14,720
B-But why so suddenly?

367
00:17:15,010 --> 00:17:18,560
That pushed it
over the edge

368
00:17:15,150 --> 00:17:17,630
We just had an earthquake, remember?

369
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:21,140
<i>Right, we did.</i>

370
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:28,400
<i>What's Mizuhara thinking right now?</i>

371
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:30,300
What's with the pause?

372
00:17:28,690 --> 00:17:32,360
Wassup?

373
00:17:29,190 --> 00:17:32,360
Were you overseas?

374
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:32,820
Yeah, that was a pretty big one!

375
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:35,580
Wait, so we're supposed to move?

376
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:37,200
That's too sudden!

377
00:17:37,610 --> 00:17:40,820
Apparently, it's fine to leave the 
furniture and move it some other time.

378
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:43,860
But for now, the landlord 
wants us to take our essentials

379
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:46,290
Ask the landlord
for details

380
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:46,290
and stay somewhere else starting tonight.

381
00:17:46,290 --> 00:17:49,130
Tonight? That's impossible.

382
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:51,580
I tried to negotiate,

383
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:54,380
but he said he'd pay us extra to move out.

384
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:55,850
10 months' rent

385
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:55,850
B-But...

386
00:17:56,270 --> 00:17:59,680
There's no law that forces us to move,

387
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:02,660
but apparently it's unsafe for real.

388
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:07,690
The owner decided it'd be better 
to be safe than sorry.

389
00:18:09,210 --> 00:18:11,900
<i>This apartment building's going away?</i>

390
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:14,410
<i>I have to move? Seriously?</i>

391
00:18:14,410 --> 00:18:16,740
<i>I can't live in my place anymore?</i>

392
00:18:17,230 --> 00:18:20,330
<i>But that means saying goodbye to Mizuhara.</i>

393
00:18:20,610 --> 00:18:23,950
<i>No!</i>

394
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:24,620
It's over!!

395
00:18:21,370 --> 00:18:24,620
Celebrating
homelessness!

396
00:18:25,860 --> 00:18:27,110
Okay, bye!

397
00:18:27,110 --> 00:18:30,380
If anything comes up, I'll drop it 
in the group chat we just made.

398
00:18:28,090 --> 00:18:30,380
Who could've seen
this coming?

399
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:30,380
Life is strange,
and I feel alive

400
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:33,090
<i>Wait, who are you?!</i>

401
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:37,470
Karaoke or something

402
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,600
Wanna pull an all-nighter, 
all three of us?

403
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:36,990
Uh, why would we?

404
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:40,350
You must have
lots of friends

405
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:40,450
I don't think you'll have trouble 
finding a place to go.

406
00:18:40,450 --> 00:18:46,030
If I come bearing the viral melon bread, 
I can stay for a whole week.

407
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:46,520
I pinged one of my
cosplayer friends earlier

408
00:18:46,490 --> 00:18:47,660
You, Master?

409
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:48,820
Family home.

410
00:18:48,820 --> 00:18:50,110
And you, Mizuhara-san?

411
00:18:50,530 --> 00:18:53,190
I think I'll go back to my 
family home for now, too.

412
00:18:53,190 --> 00:18:55,100
I don't know after that.

413
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:58,430
That moving-out fee will help 
with living expenses, too.

414
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:03,160
You're so positive,
it's almost psycho

415
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:01,070
You're so quick to change gears.

416
00:19:01,070 --> 00:19:03,160
Better that than getting buried alive.

417
00:19:03,850 --> 00:19:05,290
Okay, see you.

418
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:10,590
She's so blasé.

419
00:19:09,040 --> 00:19:10,590
What about
our all-nighter?

420
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:12,550
<i>Mizuhara...</i>

421
00:19:12,990 --> 00:19:16,620
<i>For real? Are we seriously 
gonna part like this?</i>

422
00:19:16,620 --> 00:19:19,520
<i>Doesn't Mizuhara feel sad about this?</i>

423
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:22,030
<i>You lived here for two years.</i>

424
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:24,270
<i>Your entire college life was here.</i>

425
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:27,440
<i>We met here at this place.</i>

426
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:31,650
<i>It's not like I don't believe she'll 
actually look into her feelings.</i>

427
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:35,050
<i>We still go to the same college, 
and I have her contact info.</i>

428
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:40,070
<i>But we won't be able to run into 
each other at home like we used to.</i>

429
00:19:40,410 --> 00:19:42,590
Let's be neighbors, fair and square.

430
00:19:42,590 --> 00:19:46,580
<i>Nothing good comes of us 
not being neighbors anymore.</i>

431
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:50,540
<i>Honestly, if we were actually dating,</i>

432
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:53,130
<i>I'd suggest living together right now.</i>

433
00:19:53,690 --> 00:19:56,720
<i>Mizuhara... Mizuhara!</i>

434
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:59,660
<i>But there's nothing I can do.</i>

435
00:19:59,660 --> 00:20:01,300
I'll get going, too.

436
00:20:00,510 --> 00:20:02,560
Cruel world!!

437
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:19,320
dun

438
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:21,280
Wait, who is this?

439
00:20:21,610 --> 00:20:24,990
This is Saifur. 
He's from the Philippines.

440
00:20:25,470 --> 00:20:26,940
Hello.

441
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:29,150
Wow, you're so big.

442
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:36,670
His name means
"Sword of truth" in Malay

443
00:20:29,150 --> 00:20:33,600
He's been working part-time at our store 
for the last month and a half.

444
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:36,860
I'm letting him stay in your room.

445
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:38,660
Wait, my room?!

446
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:40,220
Don't assume you'll
have your grandmother
and your room forever

447
00:20:37,170 --> 00:20:40,220
You're not
using it

448
00:20:38,660 --> 00:20:40,220
But of course.

449
00:20:40,220 --> 00:20:42,610
Besides, what about my angel?

450
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:44,410
If your building was being torn down,

451
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:47,460
why couldn't you suggest living together?

452
00:20:47,020 --> 00:20:48,810
This is the
problem with you

453
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:48,810
You gutless boy.

454
00:20:49,370 --> 00:20:52,080
<i>Yeah, no, I don't have unlimited courage.</i>

455
00:20:50,350 --> 00:20:56,280
Asking the impossible again...

456
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:54,710
Know that you can't stay forever.

457
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:58,950
<i>But hey, I guess that makes sense.</i>

458
00:20:58,950 --> 00:21:00,940
<i>It's been two years since I left home.</i>

459
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:00,940
He's a real hard worker.

460
00:21:00,570 --> 00:21:02,870
Time is heartless

461
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:02,870
<i>Of course everything's changing.</i>

462
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:06,830
I'll look for a new place

463
00:21:03,350 --> 00:21:06,830
<i>Everything's destroying my mental state.</i>

464
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:06,830
while I eat...

465
00:21:14,130 --> 00:21:18,520
<i>Mizuhara! Mizuhara!</i>

466
00:21:14,790 --> 00:21:19,010
Come back to me!!

467
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:19,010
Harumi-san,
is the nasi goreng done?

468
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:19,010
Almost done

469
00:21:19,010 --> 00:21:22,670
That's a lot of stuff, girl. 
Got nowhere to go?

470
00:21:22,670 --> 00:21:23,840
Leave me alone.

471
00:21:25,110 --> 00:21:26,710
You failed!

472
00:21:26,710 --> 00:21:29,100
You need to target a meeker girl.

473
00:21:27,310 --> 00:21:31,640
One who'd go
with the flow

474
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:31,640
That one's too headstrong.

475
00:23:42,970 --> 00:23:46,200
Oh, wek-a-pepo, wake up people, Ieyasu?

476
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:49,380
Use Incineroar on Garchomp. Healthy.

477
00:23:57,790 --> 00:24:00,000
Okay, you two take care.

478
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:01,520
O-Okay.

479
00:24:01,520 --> 00:24:03,300
She's so chill.

480
00:24:03,300 --> 00:24:07,150
There, there, Master. 
Let's be streamers with no address.

481
00:24:07,150 --> 00:24:07,890
No way!

482
00:24:07,890 --> 00:24:09,880
But if Mizuhara-san 
sees you on the streets,

483
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:13,260
she'll go, "I feel so bad! I need to 
marry him and take him in."

484
00:24:13,260 --> 00:24:14,770
Or not. Never.

485
00:24:14,770 --> 00:24:16,770
Have more confidence in yourself.

486
00:24:16,770 --> 00:24:18,960
Anyway, next time on <i>Rent-a-Girlfriend</i>:

487
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:19,820
"Moving and...

488
00:24:19,820 --> 00:24:20,520
...Girlfriend."

489
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:23,740
Listen, Master! Don't go 
stalking Mizuhara-san, okay?!

490
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:27,030
"Moving and Girlfriend"

491
00:24:23,740 --> 00:24:24,620
I won't!

492
00:24:24,620 --> 00:24:26,590
You're still at it?

